      <workList xml:id="workDesc_2c64c7c9">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e224221">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_7d070af5">B2:427</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_98e263ab" xml:lang="da">Latinske Cantata, indrettede i Anledning af den høye Formæling imellem Kron-Prints Gustav af Sverrig og Kron-Printsesse Sophie Magdalene af Dannemark</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_b99d6e73">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_063086e1">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
               <persName role="dedicatee" xml:id="persName_185a583f">Crown Prince Gustav of Sweden</persName>
               <persName role="dedicatee" xml:id="persName_3afd01ee">Princess Sophie Magdalene</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_dae12e86">
               <date isodate="1766" xml:id="date_e2bac22c">1766</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_89631e77">Copenhagen,</geogName>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_fd030f05">
               <p xml:id="idm96">Very little information on this cantata has survived, and even the text book seems to have been lost. There is only a brief reference to the work in an article in the newspaper<rend xml:id="idm97" fontstyle="italic"> Kiøbenhavns Adresse-Contoirs Efterretninger</rend> noting that it was to be performed at The Musical Society on 2 October 1766 celebrating the marriage of the crown prince of Sweden, <persName xml:id="idm98" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Gustav</persName>, to <persName xml:id="idm99" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Princess Sophie Magdalene</persName> of Denmark. There is no indication as to whom the author of the text is, only that the text is in Latin. The newspaper mentions that ‘thanks are due to the famous Kapellmeister, Mr. Scheibe, for composing the music which in all instances has entirely met the intentions of the poet, giving his thoughts the strongest expression and most stately enriches and heightens them [i.e. the thoughts].’</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_68bd56be">
               <language xml:id="da">Danish</language>
            </langUsage>
            <biblList xml:id="listBibl_754e6bff-9d81-49fc-8e2f-ff868b73dde8259">
               <head xml:id="head_53f1e460">Bibliography</head>
               <bibl label="" xml:id="bibl_d381b49b">
                  <genre xml:id="genre_24d3e427">article</genre>
                  <genre xml:id="genre_b0b84826">newspaper</genre>
                  <annot xml:id="annot_3ace20a2">
                     <p xml:id="idm108">
                        <lb xml:id="idm109"/>'I Morgen viser det Musikalske Selskab i Raadhuus-Strædet sin allerunderdanigste Beredvillighed imod det Høy-Kongelige Huus ved nogle Latinske Cantata, indrettede i Anledning af den høye Formæling imellem Deres Kongelige Høyheder Kron-Prints Gustav af Sverrig og Kron-Printsesse Sophie Magdalene af Dannemark. Compositionen af Musiqven har man den berømte Hr. Capel-Mester Scheibe at takke for, hvilken i Alting har paa det nøyeste opfyldt Poetens Hensigter, i at give hans Tanker den stærkeste Eftertryk, og paa det prægtigste berige og forhøye dem.'</p>
                  </annot>
                  <title level="a" xml:id="title_d84db3dc">Adskilligt Nyt</title>
                  <title level="j" xml:id="title_824254af">Kiøbenhavns Adresse-Contoirs Efterretninger</title>
                  <imprint xml:id="imprint_f7402111">
                     <date isodate="1766-10-01" xml:id="date_54102000">1766-10-01</date>
                  </imprint>
               </bibl>
            </biblList>
